--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFE: fine padding loops*: `padP` / `unpadP` (KIL6Pad) run through `KFD.fcode`: every counted loop is a unary loop, so
--   the per-element cost is `O(1)` for bit data and the per-block loop overhead is
--   `O(zsz (F'·Y))`, bounded by the block length.  Result: fine cost
--   `cPadF V Bb = 2000 (Bb + 2) + 20000 V` (`V` the padded volume) in place of
--   `cPad V Bb = 10^5 (V+1)(Bb+2)`.
